Krita Nova 79 - Select Shapes and the selection tools work across layer types

The Select Shapes tool (the arrow) on a paint layer, or any layer without
vector shapes, drags a rectangular pixel selection instead of showing
"This tool only works on vector layers". It uses the selection tools'
modifiers: Shift adds, Alt subtracts, Shift+Alt intersects. A click
without a drag deselects.

On a vector layer, a click with no modifier keys on a shape with the
rectangle, ellipse, freehand, polygonal or Bezier selection tool selects
that shape and switches to the Select Shapes tool when the button is
released. A click on empty canvas, or with Shift/Alt/Ctrl held, makes a
pixel selection as before. Magic wand, similar color and magnetic
selection are not changed, since they work on colors.

